hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"2869","**\nNarrated to us Muhammad ibn Bashshar, narrated to us Abd al-Wahhab, narrated to us Ayyub, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Qasim, on the authority of al-Qasim, on the authority of Aisha (RA), who said:\n\Sawdah (RA) was a heavy woman who walked slowly. She sought permission from the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) to depart from Muzdalifah to Mina at night"," and he permitted her to do so.\""\n\nAisha (RA) said: \""I wish I had sought permission from the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) just as Sawdah (RA) did. For indeed"," Aisha (RA) would only depart from Muzdalifah with the Imam.\"""""
